  "prefLabel": "Nur 302.06 Qualifications for a Medication Nursing Assistant Certificate",
  "priorExpiration": "2023-03-22",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Nur 302.06 Qualifications for a Medication Nursing Assistant Certificate. Each applicant for an initial medication nursing assistant certificate shall:\n\n(a) Possess a current unencumbered LNA license issued by the OPLC;\n\n(b) Successfully complete a board-approved medication administration education program described in Nur 800; and\n\n(c) Pass the required the competency evaluation described in Nur 800.\n\nSource. #8873, eff 4-24-07; ss by #10298, eff 3-22-13, EXPIRED: 3-22-23\n\nNew. #13886, eff 4-22-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/nur100-800.html"
